=== Elections in the 2000s ===
A by-election was held in November 2009, caused by the resignation of former Speaker of the House of Commons Michael Martin. Labour won fairly comfortably, compared to the surprising SNP win in the neighbouring constituency of [[Glasgow East (UK Parliament constituency)|Glasgow East]] in the previous year. The turnout was the lowest in Scottish history.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/newstopics/byelection/6561863/Labour-can-win-fourth-general-election-after-Glasgow-North-East.html |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20091116141930/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/newstopics/byelection/6561863/Labour-can-win-fourth-general-election-after-Glasgow-North-East.html |url-status=dead |archive-date=16 November 2009 |work=The Telegraph |title=Labour 'can win fourth general election after Glasgow North East' |first=Simon |last=Johnson |date=13 November 2009 |access-date=3 May 2010}}</ref>

