{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}} {{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Angus and Perthshire Glens|parliament=uk|image=[[File:AngusPerthshireGlens2024Constituency.svg|258px]]|caption=Boundary of Angus and Perthshire Glens in [[Scotland]]|map_entity=Scotland|map_year=|year=[[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]]|abolished=|type=County|previous=[[Angus (UK Parliament constituency)|Angus]], [[Dundee East (UK Parliament constituency)|Dundee East]], [[Dundee West (UK Parliament constituency)|Dundee West]], [[Ochil and South Perthshire]] and [[Perth and North Perthshire]]|next=|electorate=|mp=[[Dave Doogan]]|party=[[Scottish National Party|SNP]]|region=Scotland|county=[[Perth and Kinross]], [[Angus, Scotland|Angus]]|european=|elects_howmany=One|towns=[[Brechin]], [[Forfar]], [[Montrose, Angus|Montrose]]}}'''Angus and Perthshire Glens''' is a [[county constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom]] used since the [[2024 United Kingdom general election]]. It elects one [[Member of Parliament (MP)]] by the [[first past the post]] system of [[election]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=28 June 2023 - 2023 Review Report laid before Parliament {{!}} The Boundary Commission for Scotland |url=https://www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk/?q=resources/news/28-june-2023-2023-review-report-laid-parliament |access-date=2023-06-29 |website=www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref>
== Boundaries == {{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Angus and Perthshire Glens (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}} As a result of the Sixth Periodical Review of the [[Boundary Commission for Scotland]], the constituency will cover northern parts of the [[Perth and Kinross]] and [[Angus, Scotland|Angus]] Council areas.<ref>[https://www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk/sites/default/files/2023_review_final/bcs_2023_review_report_web_version.pdf Boundary Commission Scotland 2023 Review Report]</ref>
It includes the Highland, Strathtay, Strathmore, and Blairgowrie & Glens wards from Perth and Kinross; and the Brechin & Edzell, Montrose & District, Forfar & District, and Kirriemuir & Dean wards from Angus.<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Angus and Perthshire Glens |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Angus%20and%20Perthshire%20Glens |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref> It also includes northern suburbs of [[Dundee]] like [[Bridgefoot, Angus|Bridgefoot]] and [[Birkhill, Angus|Birkhill]].
The boundaries are very similar to the old [[North Tayside (UK Parliament constituency)|North Tayside]] parliamentary constituency, which was a [[safe seat|safe]] [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative]] seat from its creation at the [[1983 United Kingdom general election]] until being won by the SNP in [[1997 United Kingdom general election|1997]].
