'''North East Fife''' is a [[county constituency]] in [[Fife]], Scotland, represented in the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]] by [[Wendy Chamberlain]] of the [[Scottish Liberal Democrats|Liberal Democrats]] since the [[2019 United Kingdom general election|2019 general election]].

The seat was created in 1983, and was held by the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservative Party]] for four years, before being represented by [[Menzies Campbell]] from 1987 to 2015. Campbell was elected as a member of the [[Liberal Party (UK)|Liberal Party]], which later merged with the [[Social Democratic Party (UK)|Social Democratic Party]] to form the Liberal Democrats. At the [[2015 United Kingdom general election|2015 general election]], the seat was gained by [[Stephen Gethins]] of the [[Scottish National Party]] (SNP). Gethins held his seat at the [[2017 United Kingdom general election|2017 general election]] by just two votes over Elizabeth Riches of the Liberal Democrats, making the seat the most [[marginal seat|marginal]] in the United Kingdom. At the [[2019 United Kingdom general election|2019 general election]], Chamberlain defeated Gethins to regain the seat for the Liberal Democrats; this was the SNP's only loss at the general election.

== Boundaries ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/North East Fife (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of current boundaries}}
'''1983–2005''': North East Fife District.

'''2005–present''': The area of the Fife Council other than those parts in the constituencies of Dunfermline and West Fife, Glenrothes, and Kirkcaldy and Cowdenbeath.

North East Fife constituency is in the region of Fife in Scotland. Fife has the River Tay on its northern coast, and the [[Firth of Forth]] to the south. The famous golf and university town of [[St Andrews]] is the major settlement in the seat. Others include [[Cupar]], [[Newport-on-Tay]], [[Newburgh, Fife|Newburgh]], [[Auchtermuchty]], and [[Anstruther]].

