North East Fife was the most [[marginal seat|marginal]] result in the country at the [[2017 United Kingdom general election|2017 general election]], with incumbent SNP MP [[Stephen Gethins]] seeing his majority cut from 4,344 votes (9.6%) to 2 votes (0.004%) ahead of the [[Scottish Liberal Democrats|Liberal Democrat]] candidate, Elizabeth Riches. An alike result in [[Winchester (UK Parliament constituency)#Elections in the 1990s|Winchester]] at the [[1997 United Kingdom general election|1997 general election]] was adjudicated and declared void and resulted in a legislative change in party naming rules (the [[Registration of Political Parties Act 1998]]).<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-scotland-scotland-politics-40214545 | title=General election 2017: SNP wins Fife North East seat by just two votes |publisher=[[BBC]] |date=2017-06-09 |access-date=2017-06-15}}</ref>

