{{Short description|Parliamentary constituency in the United Kingdom, 2024 onwards}}
{{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Aberdeenshire North and Moray East|parliament=uk|image=[[File:AberdeenshireNorthMorayEast2024Constituency.svg|258px]]|caption=Boundary of Aberdeenshire North and Moray East in [[Scotland]]|map_entity=Scotland|map_year=2024|year=[[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]]|abolished=|type=County|previous=[[Banff and Buchan (UK Parliament constituency)|Banff and Buchan]] & [[Moray (UK Parliament constituency)|Moray]]|next=|electorate=|mp=[[Seamus Logan]]|party=[[Scottish National Party|SNP]]|region=Scotland|county=[[Aberdeenshire]] and [[Moray]]|european=|elects_howmany=One}}'''Aberdeenshire North and Moray East''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=28 June 2023 - 2023 Review Report laid before Parliament {{!}} The Boundary Commission for Scotland |url=https://www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk/?q=resources/news/28-june-2023-2023-review-report-laid-parliament |access-date=2023-06-29 |website=www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Following the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it was first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].

The seat is currently held by [[Seamus Logan]] of the [[Scottish National Party]] since the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].

== History ==
Following a significant illness and period in hospital, [[David Duguid (politician)|David Duguid]], the incumbent MP for the constituency's predecessor Banff and Buchan, was informed that he had not been selected as the Conservative candidate on the evening of 5 June 2024. This was in spite of being previously selected by his local constituency association and indicating he was fit to stand.<ref>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c3ggj3ql5r4o</ref>

Although he had previously said that he was stepping down from Westminster, [[Scottish Conservatives]] leader [[Douglas Ross (Scottish politician)|Douglas Ross]] announced that he would be the candidate on the morning of the 6 June, with nomination deadline falling on 7 June.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2024-06-05 |title=Former minister David Duguid not selected to stand in election |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c977x2ldv7eo |access-date=2024-06-05 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>

Labour candidate Andy Brown was suspended on 19 June 2024 following allegations that he questioned Russia's involvement in the [[Salisbury poisonings]] and downplayed the level of [[antisemitism in the Labour party]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Labour suspends candidate over 'pro-Russian' post |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c0vvjzw5ejno |accessdate=19 June 2024 |website=BBC}}
</ref>

== Contents ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Aberdeenshire North and Moray East (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency comprises the following wards of [[Aberdeenshire]] and [[Moray]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Aberdeenshire North and Moray East |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Aberdeenshire%20North%20and%20Moray%20East |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=[[Electoral Calculus]]}}</ref>

The vast majority of the constituency comes from the [[Banff and Buchan (UK Parliament constituency)|Banff and Buchan constituency]].

*In full: From Aberdeenshire Council the wards of Banff and District, Troup, Fraserburgh and District, Peterhead North and Rattray, Peterhead South and Cruden; from Moray Council the wards of Keith and Cullen, and Buckie;
*In part: from Aberdeenshire Council the ward of Central Buchan; from Moray Council the ward of Fochabers Lhanbryde<ref>[https://www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk/reviews/2023-review-uk-parliament-constituencies 2023 Review UK Parliament constituencies] Boundary Commission for Scotland</ref>

