{{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Alloa and Grangemouth|parliament=uk|image=[[File:AlloaGrangemouth2024Constituency.svg|258px]]|caption=Boundary of Alloa and Grangemouth in [[Scotland]]|map_entity=Scotland|map_year=|year=[[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]]|abolished=|type=County|previous=[[Ochil and South Perthshire (UK Parliament constituency)|Ochil and South Perthshire]], [[Falkirk (UK Parliament constituency)|Falkirk]] & [[Linlithgow and East Falkirk (UK Parliament constituency)|Linlithgow and East Falkirk]]|next=|electorate=70,680|mp=[[Brian Leishman]]|party=[[Labour]]|region=Scotland|county=[[Clackmannanshire]], [[Perthshire]], [[Falkirk]]|european=|elects_howmany=One|towns=[[Alloa]], [[Clackmannan]], [[Grangemouth]]}}'''Alloa and Grangemouth''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=28 June 2023 - 2023 Review Report laid before Parliament {{!}} The Boundary Commission for Scotland |url=https://www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk/?q=resources/news/28-june-2023-2023-review-report-laid-parliament |access-date=2023-06-29 |website=www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Following the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it was first contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].

The seat has been held by [[Brian Leishman]] of the [[Scottish Labour|Labour Party]] since the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].

