The constituency name refers to the town of [[Hamilton, South Lanarkshire|Hamilton]] and the valley of the [[River Clyde]] south of [[Glasgow]].

== Contents ==
{{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Hamilton and Clyde Valley (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}}
The constituency will comprise the following wards of [[South Lanarkshire]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Hamilton and Clyde Valley |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Hamilton%20and%20Clyde%20Valley |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>

* [[Clydesdale South (ward)|Clydesdale South]] from the [[East Kilbride, Strathaven and Lesmahagow (UK Parliament constituency)|East Kilbride, Strathaven and Lesmahagow constituency]]
* [[Clydesdale North (ward)|Clydesdale North]], [[Clydesdale West (ward)|Clydesdale West]], [[Hamilton North and East (ward)|Hamilton North and East]], [[Hamilton South (ward)|Hamilton South]] and [[Larkhall (South Lanarkshire ward)|Larkhall]] from the [[Lanark and Hamilton East (UK Parliament constituency)|Lanark and Hamilton East constituency]]
* [[Hamilton West and Earnock (ward)|Hamilton West and Earnock]] from the [[Rutherglen and Hamilton West (UK Parliament constituency)|Rutherglen and Hamilton West constituency]]

