{{Short description|United Kingdom parliamentary constituency}} {{Infobox UK constituency main|name=Mid Dunbartonshire|parliament=uk|image=[[File:MidDunbartonshire2024Constituency.svg|258px]]|caption=Boundary of Mid Dunbartonshire in [[Scotland]]|map_entity=Scotland|map_year=2024|year=[[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]]|abolished=|type=County|previous=[[East Dunbartonshire (UK Parliament constituency)|East Dunbartonshire]]|next=|electorate=|mp=[[Susan Murray]]|party=[[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]]|region=Scotland|county=[[East Dunbartonshire]]|european=|elects_howmany=One|towns=[[Bearsden]], [[Bishopbriggs]], [[Kirkintilloch]], [[Lenzie]], [[Milngavie]]}}'''Mid Dunbartonshire''' is a [[List of UK Parliament constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] in the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom|UK Parliament]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=28 June 2023 - 2023 Review Report laid before Parliament {{!}} The Boundary Commission for Scotland |url=https://www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk/?q=resources/news/28-june-2023-2023-review-report-laid-parliament |access-date=2023-06-29 |website=www.bcomm-scotland.independent.gov.uk}}</ref> Further to the completion of the [[2023 Periodic Review of Westminster constituencies]], it will first be contested at the [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024 general election]].
== Boundaries == {{maplink|raw={{Wikipedia:Map data/Mid Dunbartonshire (UK Parliament constituency)}}|frame=yes|frame-height=250|text=Map of boundaries from 2024}} The constituency will comprise the following wards of the [[East Dunbartonshire]]:<ref>{{Cite web |title=New Seat Details - Mid Dunbartonshire |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Mid%20Dunbartonshire |access-date=2023-07-29 |website=www.electoralcalculus.co.uk}}</ref>
* [[Bearsden North (ward)|Bearsden North]], [[Bearsden South (ward)|Bearsden South]], [[Bishopbriggs South]] and [[Milngavie (ward)|Milngavie]] from the [[East Dunbartonshire (UK Parliament constituency)|East Dunbartonshire constituency]] * As well as the minority parts of wards of [[Bishopbriggs North and Campsie (ward)|Bishopbriggs North and Campsie]], [[Kirkintilloch East and North and Twechar (ward)|Kirkintilloch East and North and Twechar]] and [[Lenzie and Kirkintilloch South (ward)|Lenzie and Kirkintilloch South]] from the [[Cumbernauld, Kilsyth and Kirkintilloch East (UK Parliament constituency)|Cumbernauld, Kilsyth and Kirkintilloch East constituency]] * Part of [[Bishopbriggs South]] from the [[Glasgow North East (UK Parliament constituency)|Glasgow North East constituency]]
==Constituency profile== [[Electoral Calculus]] characterises the proposed seat as "Strong Left", with left-wing economic and socially liberal views, high levels of university education and an internationalist outlook including strong opposition to [[Brexit]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/calcwork23.py?seat=Mid%20Dunbartonshire | title=Electoral Calculus }}</ref>
