'''Edinburgh South West''' is a Scottish [[United Kingdom constituencies|constituency]] of the [[House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons]] of the [[Parliament of the United Kingdom]], first used at the [[2005 United Kingdom general election|2005 UK general election]]. It elects one [[Member of Parliament (MP)]] by the [[first past the post system]] of election. Since [[2024 United Kingdom general election|2024]], it has been represented by [[Scott Arthur]] of the [[Scottish Labour|Labour Party]].

==Constituency profile==
Edinburgh South West covers a south western portion of the city around the Lanark Road. It has an urban north east including [[Gorgie]] and [[Slateford]], and a suburban centre including [[Wester Hailes]]. The southwest part is rural and extends into the [[Pentland Hills]].

The seat is left-leaning and pro-EU, with wealthier residents than the UK average.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/seatdetails.py?seat=Edinburgh+South+West |title=Edinburgh South West: Seat Details |website=Electoral Calculus |access-date=9 November 2021 |archive-date=9 November 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211109120320/https://www.electoralcalculus.co.uk/fcgi-bin/seatdetails.py?seat=Edinburgh+South+West |url-status=live }}</ref>

== Boundaries ==
Edinburgh South West is one of five constituencies covering the [[City of Edinburgh council area]]. All are entirely within the city council area.

Prior to the 2005 general election, the city area had been covered by six constituencies and, of the six, there was one, [[Edinburgh East and Musselburgh (UK Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh East and Musselburgh]], which straddled the boundary with the [[East Lothian council area]], to include [[Musselburgh]].

Edinburgh South West is mostly a replacement for the former [[Edinburgh Pentlands (UK Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh Pentlands]] constituency, but excludes some of the east of that constituency. Also, it includes a south western portion of the former [[Edinburgh Central (UK Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh Central]] constituency.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.bcomm-scotland.gov.uk/ |title=Fifth Periodical Review |publisher=[[Boundary Commission for Scotland]] |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070921124603/http://www.bcomm-scotland.gov.uk/ |archive-date=21 September 2007}}</ref> The [[Scottish Parliament]] uses different boundaries. Edinburgh South West is mostly contained within the [[Edinburgh Pentlands (Scottish Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh Pentlands]] constituency for elections to the Scottish Parliament, with some parts of the north and east of the seat being located in the constituencies of [[Edinburgh Central (Scottish Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh Central]], [[Edinburgh Southern (Scottish Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh Southern]] and [[Edinburgh Western (Scottish Parliament constituency)|Edinburgh Western]].

The constituency comprises the following [[ward (politics)|wards]] of the [[City of Edinburgh Council]] which were used in elections to the council at the time of the constituency's first contest in 2005: [[Balerno]], [[Baberton]], [[Colinton]], [[Craiglockhart]], [[Dalry, Edinburgh|Dalry]], [[Firrhill, Edinburgh|Firrhill]], [[Fountainbridge]], [[Moat, Edinburgh|Moat]], [[Murrayburn]], [[Parkhead, Edinburgh|Parkhead]], [[Shandon, Edinburgh|Shandon]] and [[Sighthill, Edinburgh|Sighthill]]. As a result of the [[Local Governance (Scotland) Act 2004]], these wards were replaced with new wards in 2007. Current ward boundaries are not aligned with the constituency boundaries.

